WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.265
A strong bid starts long before the first page is

00:00:04.265 --> 00:00:08.529
written. BidStream brings opportunity discovery, company evidence
and proposal preparation

00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:12.794
into one focused workspace. Follow Nordway Transport Consulting
from a

00:00:12.794 --> 00:00:17.059
promising notice to a coordinated response. The dashboard keeps
deadlines

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:21.324
and next actions visible, while each pursuit brings its
documents,

00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:25.588
specialists and decisions together. Start here to see what
deserves

00:00:25.588 --> 00:00:29.000
attention, and where your team should move next.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.328
Open the profile menu in the upper right, then choose

00:00:34.328 --> 00:00:38.657
Companies. Select Nordway Transport Consulting and open its
company profile.

00:00:38.657 --> 00:00:42.985
This is where reusable bid knowledge begins. Add the business

00:00:42.985 --> 00:00:47.313
website, years in operation and contact email, then upload the

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:51.642
company profile document. Keep the address aligned with the team

00:00:51.642 --> 00:00:55.970
handling buyer correspondence. Save the profile so that future
pursuits

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.000
can draw on the same company information.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.203
Build out Nordway's evidence library with the documents a buyer

00:01:04.203 --> 00:01:08.406
may request: financial reports, project references, client
testimonials, team qualifications

00:01:08.406 --> 00:01:12.609
and legal records. Choose the right document category before
uploading

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:16.812
each group. Open a file to inspect its readable content,

00:01:16.812 --> 00:01:21.014
and correct its category when needed. Keeping evidence organised
now

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:25.217
gives your team a stronger starting point when a new

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:29.000
opportunity arrives, without rebuilding the company story every
time.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.203
The evidence coverage panel shows which parts of the company

00:01:34.203 --> 00:01:38.406
library are represented and where to improve next. Follow the

00:01:38.406 --> 00:01:42.609
suggested actions to add comparable projects, current
registrations or relevant

00:01:42.609 --> 00:01:46.812
expert qualifications. Open the explanation to understand what
strengthens an

00:01:46.812 --> 00:01:51.014
expression of interest. Then expand matching preferences and
company details

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:55.217
to refine capabilities and target markets. Save the changes,
keeping

00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:59.000
both discovery and preparation grounded in a company profile.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.203
Every company can bring its own AI workspace into BidStream.

00:02:04.203 --> 00:02:08.406
Here, Nordway uses the connected ChatGPT account for its
preparation.

00:02:08.406 --> 00:02:12.609
Open Integrations from the profile menu, sign in and enable

00:02:12.609 --> 00:02:16.812
the BidStream connection in ChatGPT. Send a pursuit’s document
package,

00:02:16.812 --> 00:02:21.014
work with your assistant, then return the analysis and drafts

00:02:21.014 --> 00:02:25.217
for review. Company documents and results stay organised within
the

00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:29.000
right workspace, while each company chooses its own connection.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.328
Open Discover to explore opportunities from the World Bank and

00:02:34.328 --> 00:02:38.657
TED feeds. Search for a service such as road safety

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:42.985
or transport planning, then narrow the results by market or

00:02:42.985 --> 00:02:47.313
source. Use the relevance and sorting controls to focus your

00:02:47.313 --> 00:02:51.642
review. For Nordway, the goal is a manageable set of

00:02:51.642 --> 00:02:55.970
opportunities aligned with its capabilities. Refresh sources when
needed, and

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:59.000
bring promising notices into view before preparation.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.203
Open a notice to understand why it matches Nordway. Review

00:03:04.203 --> 00:03:08.406
the capability and geography signals alongside the buyer's scope,
then

00:03:08.406 --> 00:03:12.609
follow the source link for the original procurement details. The

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:16.812
deadline display makes timing visible: green, amber and red are

00:03:16.812 --> 00:03:21.014
paired with clear labels and dates. Use those signals to

00:03:21.014 --> 00:03:25.217
separate work you can plan from work that needs attention,

00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:29.000
and confirm the buyer's exact closing time before proceeding.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.265
When a notice deserves review, click Shortlist. The opportunity
moves

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:38.529
into Nordway's pursuit pipeline, keeping the decision connected
to the

00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:42.794
notice you reviewed. Open Shortlist to compare the selected
opportunities

00:03:42.794 --> 00:03:47.059
and enter the one you want to develop. This small

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:51.324
step changes the task from scanning the market to preparing

00:03:51.324 --> 00:03:55.588
a response. Keep the shortlist focused on assignments your team

00:03:55.588 --> 00:03:59.000
has the capacity and evidence to pursue well.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.265
Return to Dashboard to plan your next steps. Submission and

00:04:04.265 --> 00:04:08.529
response counts sit above the next action list, where deadline

00:04:08.529 --> 00:04:12.794
and stage help prioritise each pursuit. Filter for drafting or

00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:17.059
awaiting response to focus. Open an action to continue the

00:04:17.059 --> 00:04:21.324
work in context. Direct tenders can enter the same pipeline,

00:04:21.324 --> 00:04:25.588
giving your team a route forward whether the buyer requests

00:04:25.588 --> 00:04:29.000
an initial expression of interest or a tender.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.203
Inside the pursuit, upload the tender, terms of reference and

00:04:34.203 --> 00:04:38.406
supporting attachments. Choose the procurement route and add your
priorities

00:04:38.406 --> 00:04:42.609
for the response. Send the document package, then open ChatGPT

00:04:42.609 --> 00:04:46.812
and request an analysis of requirements, qualification
prerequisites and the

00:04:46.812 --> 00:04:51.014
buyer’s chapter structure. Return to BidStream and get the
analysis

00:04:51.014 --> 00:04:55.217
and drafts. Review and apply the results to create a

00:04:55.217 --> 00:04:59.000
shared brief, with source quotations supporting each important
requirement.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.203
Open Requirements to inspect the extracted criteria. Read each
source

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:08.406
quotation, check the buyer's wording and confirm any supplied
evaluation

00:05:08.406 --> 00:05:12.609
weight. Keep mandatory requirements distinct from scored
criteria, and refine

00:05:12.609 --> 00:05:16.812
the evidence notes that will support the response. This makes

00:05:16.812 --> 00:05:21.014
the buyer's expectations visible before drafting begins. When a
requirement

00:05:21.014 --> 00:05:25.217
needs clarification, resolve it against the source document so
that

00:05:25.217 --> 00:05:29.000
the team works from the same interpretation and priorities.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.203
Open Prerequisites to see which qualification gates need
attention. BidStream

00:05:34.203 --> 00:05:38.406
suggests company evidence that may support each requirement and
explains

00:05:38.406 --> 00:05:42.609
the connection. Inspect the documents and the exact threshold
before

00:05:42.609 --> 00:05:46.812
changing a status to Verified. A readable financial report, for

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:51.014
example, needs to demonstrate the requested period and capacity.
Use

00:05:51.014 --> 00:05:55.217
Missing and Needs review to keep unresolved work visible, then

00:05:55.217 --> 00:05:59.000
close gaps with evidence your reviewers can stand behind.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.265
Open Agents to inspect the recommended specialists and drill into

00:06:04.265 --> 00:06:08.529
their assignments. Refine the brief around Nordway’s delivery
approach and

00:06:08.529 --> 00:06:12.794
select the internal experts whose qualifications support the
response. Send

00:06:12.794 --> 00:06:17.059
the updated package to your connected conversation and ask the

00:06:17.059 --> 00:06:21.324
assistant to coordinate the specialist contributions. Get the
results back

00:06:21.324 --> 00:06:25.588
in BidStream, review each contribution and apply the work you

00:06:25.588 --> 00:06:29.000
want to carry forward into the combined response.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.265
When your evidence and specialist contributions are ready, send
the

00:06:34.265 --> 00:06:38.529
updated pursuit package to the connected conversation. Ask for an

00:06:38.529 --> 00:06:42.794
expression of interest or a direct tender response, following the

00:06:42.794 --> 00:06:47.059
buyer’s structure and your company evidence. Return to BidStream,
get

00:06:47.059 --> 00:06:51.324
the analysis and drafts, then review and apply the response.

00:06:51.324 --> 00:06:55.588
Open Draft to refine the wording, complete targeted inputs and

00:06:55.588 --> 00:06:59.000
sharpen Nordway’s differentiators before downloading for your
reviewers.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.265
Open Submission sheet to turn the buyer's requested structure
into

00:07:04.265 --> 00:07:08.529
a response package. Review the table of contents and adjust

00:07:08.529 --> 00:07:12.794
each chapter to match the tender. The folder plan separates

00:07:12.794 --> 00:07:17.059
technical material, financial information, signed forms and
correspondence, with the

00:07:17.059 --> 00:07:21.324
technical chapters nested under their own section. Download the
plan

00:07:21.324 --> 00:07:25.588
to organise files consistently. See what belongs where, and keep

00:07:25.588 --> 00:07:29.000
commercial material separate while developing the technical
narrative.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.203
Send the latest pursuit package with your saved draft to

00:07:34.203 --> 00:07:38.406
the connected conversation. Ask the assistant to evaluate the
response

00:07:38.406 --> 00:07:42.609
against the buyer’s criteria, explaining each rating and
identifying evidence

00:07:42.609 --> 00:07:46.812
gaps. Get the assessment back in BidStream, review and apply

00:07:46.812 --> 00:07:51.014
it, then open Evaluate to inspect the findings. Challenge the

00:07:51.014 --> 00:07:55.217
reasoning, refine reviewer ratings and return to Draft to
strengthen

00:07:55.217 --> 00:07:59.000
the sections that need attention before the final review.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.203
In the connected conversation, ask your assistant to research
comparable

00:08:04.203 --> 00:08:08.406
awards using the pursuit’s scope, buyer and location. Request
direct

00:08:08.406 --> 00:08:12.609
source links and an explanation of why each comparison matters.

00:08:12.609 --> 00:08:16.812
Bring the findings back through Get analysis and drafts, then

00:08:16.812 --> 00:08:21.014
review the research and its citations before applying it. Add

00:08:21.014 --> 00:08:25.217
your assessment of positioning, partnerships and differentiation,
giving Nordway a

00:08:25.217 --> 00:08:29.000
documented basis for an informed decision about this opportunity.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.203
Return to Submission sheet for the final attachment check.
Confirm

00:08:34.203 --> 00:08:38.406
the required forms, signatures and qualification evidence, then
assemble the

00:08:38.406 --> 00:08:42.609
package using the chapter structure. After submitting through the
buyer's

00:08:42.609 --> 00:08:46.812
required channel, open Submission and response and click Record
submission.

00:08:46.812 --> 00:08:51.014
Today's date is supplied automatically, and you can adjust it

00:08:51.014 --> 00:08:55.217
to the submission date. Add the receipt or reference to

00:08:55.217 --> 00:08:59.000
keep a record of what was submitted and when.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:04.265
Review the expected response date extracted from the buyer's
timetable

00:09:04.265 --> 00:09:08.529
when supplied, and check its source. If an unanswered response

00:09:08.529 --> 00:09:12.794
becomes seven days overdue, the workspace highlights the follow-
up. Review

00:09:12.794 --> 00:09:17.059
the buyer address, subject and message, then copy the prepared

00:09:17.059 --> 00:09:21.324
email or open your email application. When a reply arrives,

00:09:21.324 --> 00:09:25.588
save the outcome and details. A positive EOI response moves

00:09:25.588 --> 00:09:29.000
the pursuit towards preparing the next tender stage.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.203
Nordway now has a path from relevant opportunity to carefully

00:09:34.203 --> 00:09:38.406
prepared response. Build on the evidence library, use specialist
contributions

00:09:38.406 --> 00:09:42.609
to sharpen the proposal, and keep every deadline and buyer

00:09:42.609 --> 00:09:46.812
conversation in view. Return to Dashboard, open the next action

00:09:46.812 --> 00:09:51.014
and move the pursuit forward. When you expand to another

00:09:51.014 --> 00:09:55.217
company, manage its profile from the profile menu. Start with

00:09:55.217 --> 00:09:59.000
your next opportunity, and put your experience to work.
